──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The web StickyChipBar is a presentational "jump to section" pill nav: a `chips:{id,label}[]` prop, an `activeId`
local state seeded from the first chip and updated by (a) an IntersectionObserver reporting the top-most visible
section and (b) on-click, which also smooth-scrolls to the anchor. Sticky `<nav aria-label="Jump to section">`
with a horizontally-scrollable row of pill `<button>`s; the active pill gets the cyan fill + ring + aria-current.

• Composition : horizontally-scrolling Capsule pill row (web `flex gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto px-4 py-1.5`) inside a
                translucent bar (`.background(.bar)` ≈ web `bg-[var(--bg-1)]/85 backdrop-blur`) + a 1px bottom
                hairline (web `border-b`). Active pill = accent fill .15 + accent ring .30 + accent text (web
                `bg-cyan-400/15 ring-cyan-400/30 text-cyan-200`); inactive = surface fill + textSecondary (web
                `bg-[var(--surface-2)] text-[var(--text-secondary)]`). Pill metrics ported 1:1 (gap 6 / px-4 16 /
                py-1.5 6 / pill min-h-32 / px-3 12 / py-1 4 / rounded-full → Capsule).
• activeId    : `StickyChipBarProjection.resolveActiveID` is the faithful port of `useState(chips[0]?.id ?? '')`
                plus the observer/onClick `setActiveId`: a requested id is honoured only when it names a present
                chip, else the first chip is the default, else "" for an empty bar.
• selection   : layered exactly like the web — `select(_:)` is the tap (web onClick → setActiveId + the host
                scrolls via the view's `onSelect`), and `setActiveSection(id:)` is the host scroll-spy report
                (web IntersectionObserver → setActiveId). A `ScrollViewReader` keeps the active pill centred (web
                `overflow-x-auto` active tracking), animated unless Reduce Motion.
• aria        : web `aria-label="Jump to section"` → the bar container's VoiceOver label; web `aria-current="true"`
                → the active pill's `.isSelected` trait + a localized "Current section" value.
• States      : the web has populated + (empty bar). The P4 leaf contract is layered ON TOP (identical to the
                QuickNav/AiUsageCard sibling precedent, which are likewise presentational): loading (capsule
                skeletons) / empty (friendly inline row, never a blank strip) / error (retry affordance) / content,
                PLUS the orthogonal connection axis live/stale/offline (trailing freshness chip + one-shot stale
                auto-refresh; offline keeps the cached bar). Every state renders — no hidden surface.
• Data        : presentational — the bar owns no scroll content and no networking. Chips are host-supplied via the
                P1/S8 `StickyChipBarSource` seam (`StaticStickyChipBarSource` = the web `chips` prop;
                `InMemoryStickyChipBarSource` for previews/tests). The view issues no HTTP.
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (StickyChipBarStrings, table "StickyChipBar"); 11 keys = 1 web-parity
                ("Jump to section") + 10 native chrome. Zero English literals in Swift beyond the web-default
                fallbacks. Chip labels are host-supplied display data, rendered verbatim (web parity).
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted once with surface slug "StickyChipBar".
• a11y        : VoiceOver label/value/hint + .isSelected on every pill; labels on retry/refresh; Dynamic Type via
                Font.TS roles; Reduce-Motion-aware press + scroll + skeleton shimmer.

